course: dictionary
lesson: 15795
title: Everyone agrees: unanimously
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a whole group agrees, every single person says yes and nobody says no. Unanimously is the word for that. It is an adverb, so it tells you how something was done. «The class voted unanimously to plant a tree in the school garden.» The whole class voted the same way, and nobody was against it.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Voted, agreed and elected are all words about decisions, and a whole group is always involved. If even one person put a hand up to say no, the decision was not unanimous. To check your meaning, swap in «everyone agreed» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Unanimous comes from Latin words meaning one mind. So an unanimous decision is one where the whole group is of one mind. Keep it simple: it means one shared yes.
fact: Unanimously means everyone in the group agrees, and nobody is against it.
fact: «The judges agreed unanimously that Maya had won.» Every judge agreed.
fact: «The club unanimously elected Sam as captain.» Every member chose Sam.
fact: Unanimous is the adjective: «a unanimous vote» means every person voted the same way.
fact: One person saying no means the decision is not unanimous.
exercise: «The class voted unanimously to go on the trip.» What does unanimously mean here? | The vote was taken in a hurry | The teacher chose the trip alone | Most people agreed, but two said no | *Everyone agreed, and nobody said no
exercise: «The club unanimously elected Sam as captain.» Which word tells you that the whole group agreed? | Sam | Captain | Club | *Unanimously
exercise: Priya says, «Four people voted for the cake and one voted no, so the vote was unanimous.» Is Priya right? | Yes, because the cake was nice | No, because votes are never unanimous | Yes, because most people agreed | *No, one person said no, so it was not unanimous
test: «The jury agreed unanimously that the boy was innocent.» What does unanimously show? | The boy ran away | *The whole jury agreed | The jury was late | The jury was divided
test: Which sentence uses unanimously correctly? | Unanimously is the number of goals scored | The team lost, unanimously | *The team voted unanimously to try a new game | The dog barked unanimously at the cat
exam: Which statement about unanimously is true? | It means the group argued all day | *It means everyone in the group agreed and nobody was against it | It means most people agreed | It means nobody agreed
